    "text": "LIVE\nUpdated 18 min ago\nStocks to Watch: Intel, Micron, SpaceX, Oracle\n↘️ Samsung Electronics (KR:005930): The memory-chip giant tumbled 12% as the technology sell-off hit Asia. Its South Korean rival SK Hynix fell 12%, while Japan’s SoftBank Group slid 10% in Tokyo.\n↘️ Micron Technology (MU): The U.S. memory-chip maker more than 11%. Other semiconductor companies were also hammered, with Intel down more than 6% and Nvidia declining around 3% in early trading.\n↘️ SpaceX (SPCX): Elon Musk’s rocket company opened 1% lower, a day after its shares plunged 16%. SpaceX is expected to issue more than $20 billion of bonds in an offering that could price as early as today.",
